{#- Stands alone, without the shell, because a refused request must read nothing of the ledger; `address` is the one the dashboard answers. -#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Open the dashboard on localhost - Intakt</title>
    {#- Styled inline with the light and dark tokens of assets/styles/tokens.css, because the refusal must render even where the asset paths cannot be resolved. -#}
    <style>
        :root { color-scheme: light dark; --page: #F7FAF9; --ink: #0A2B23; --tint: #EEF5F2; }
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --page: #121816; --ink: #E6ECEA; --tint: #1E2826; } }
        body { margin: 0; padding: 32px; background: var(--page); color: var(--ink); font: 17px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; }
        main { max-width: 640px; }
        pre { padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--tint); overflow-x: auto; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
    <h1>Open the dashboard on localhost</h1>
    <p class="lead">Intakt answers only <code>http://{{ address }}</code>, on the machine it runs on. The dashboard has no login, so any other address could let a web page you visit act for you.</p>
    <p>From another device, open an SSH tunnel to that machine, then open <code>http://{{ address }}</code> on this device:</p>
    <pre><code>ssh -L {{ port }}:localhost:{{ port }} you@your-server</code></pre>
</main>
</body>
</html>
